## Source

All fixtures are copied from:
- `../wuffs/test/data/` (Wuffs repository)

## Files

- `bricks-color.bmp` - BMP test image; pixel-identical to `bricks-color.png`
- `bricks-color.png` - PNG test image; oracle pair for `bricks-color.bmp`
- `bricks-color.qoi` - QOI test image (160×120 RGB, sRGB colorspace); oracle
  pair is `bricks-color.png`
- `bricks-nodither.gif` - GIF (89a) test image; oracle pair is `bricks-nodither.png`
- `bricks-nodither.png` - PNG test image; oracle pair for `bricks-nodither.gif`
- `hat.jpeg` - baseline JPEG test image (90×112 RGB, no alpha)
- `bricks-color.golden.crc32` - decimal CRC-32 of the decoded `bricks-color.png`
  pixel bytes
- `hat.jpeg.golden.nia.crc32` - decimal CRC-32 of `hat.jpeg`'s decoded pixels
  re-encoded as a single-frame NIA v1-bn4 (non-premultiplied BGRA) stream,
  per `../wuffs/doc/spec/nie-spec.md`; regenerated from an independent oracle
  and checked in, never derived from the decoder under test
- `harvesters.png` - PNG test image (PNG performance gate fixture)
- `bricks-color.lossless.webp` - WebP lossless test image
- `alpha-pixels.png` - deterministic 3×1 PNG generated in-repository; its
  pixels are opaque, translucent, and fully transparent for NRGBA tests
- `alpha-pixels.qoi` - deterministic 3×1 RGBA QOI generated in-repository with
  the same opaque, translucent, and fully transparent straight-RGBA pixel
  values as `alpha-pixels.png`
- `hippopotamus.pgm` - Netpbm P5 (binary graymap) test image (36×28, maxval
  255, single-byte samples) vendored from upstream
- `hippopotamus.ppm` - Netpbm P6 (binary pixmap) test image (36×28, maxval
  255, single-byte samples) vendored from upstream
- `npbm-maxval65535.pgm` - deterministic 2×2 Netpbm P5 generated
  in-repository; two-byte big-endian samples 0x0000, 0x0100, 0x8000, 0xFFFF
- `npbm-maxval65535.ppm` - deterministic 2×2 Netpbm P6 generated
  in-repository with R=G=B triples of the same two-byte big-endian samples as
  the PGM, so P5 and P6 with equivalent sample values decode identically
- `bricks-color.tga` - TGA test image (uncompressed true-color, 160×120,
  24-bit BGR, no alpha); oracle pair is `bricks-color.png`
- `bricks-nodither.tga` - TGA test image (indexed-color, 160×120, 256-entry
  24-bit palette, 8-bit indices); oracle pair is `bricks-nodither.png`
- `bricks-gray.tga` - TGA test image (grayscale RLE, type 11, 160×120,
  8-bit samples); oracle pair is `bricks-gray.png`
- `bricks-gray.png` - PNG test image; oracle pair for `bricks-gray.tga`
- `muybridge-frame-000.wbmp` - WBMP Type 0 test image (30×20, single-byte
  width and height varints); its bitmap bits are identical to frame 0 of
  `muybridge.gif` thresholded at luminance 128 (verified against the standard
  library's `image/gif` decoder)
- `bricks-nodither.wbmp` - WBMP Type 0 test image (160×120, two-byte width
  varint, single-byte height varint); generated from `bricks-nodither.png` by
  `../wuffs/script/convert-png-to-wbmp.go` with the same gray-threshold
  semantics (bit set when luminance ≥ 128), oracle pair is `bricks-nodither.png`
- `bricks-color.etc1.pkm` - ETC1 PKM test image (160×120, RGB, PKM v0x10
  format 0x0000), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `bricks-color.etc1s.pkm` - ETC1S PKM test image (160×120, RGB, PKM v0x10
  format 0x0000; ETC1S is the ETC1 block encoding used by Basis Universal,
  produced by nigeltao's custom etc1tool), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `bricks-color.etc2.pkm` - ETC2 PKM test image (160×120, RGB, PKM v0x20
  format 0x0001), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `mona-lisa.21x32.etc2.pkm` - ETC2 PKM test image (21×32, RGB, PKM v0x20
  format 0x0001; the 24×32 extended canvas is cropped to the original 21×32
  geometry, exercising non-multiple-of-four dimensions), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data`
- `hippopotamus.masked-with-muybridge.etc2.bgra-binary.pkm` - ETC2 PKM test
  image (36×28, one-bit alpha, PKM v0x20 format 0x0004), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data`
- `hippopotamus.masked-with-muybridge.etc2.bgra-nonpremul.pkm` - ETC2 PKM
  test image (36×28, full non-premultiplied alpha, PKM v0x20 format 0x0003),
  vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `etc2.golden.manifest` - small golden manifest selecting the six vendored
  PKM fixtures and recording each fixture's reported dimensions, its PKM
  variant, and the canonical CRC-32 (IEEE) of its decoded straight RGBA
  pixels (see Checksums below)
- `49.bn4.nie` - NIE still image (16×16, v1-bn4: non-premultiplied BGRA, 4
  bytes per pixel), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `49.bn8.nie` - NIE still image (16×16, v1-bn8: non-premultiplied BGRA, 8
  bytes per pixel / 16-bit channels), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `49.bp4.nie` - NIE still image (16×16, v1-bp4: premultiplied BGRA, 4 bytes
  per pixel), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `49.bp8.nie` - NIE still image (16×16, v1-bp8: premultiplied BGRA, 8 bytes
  per pixel / 16-bit channels), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`
- `crude-flag.nie` - NIE still image (3×2, v1-bn4), the worked example from
  `../wuffs/doc/spec/nie-spec.md`: blue, white and red columns, all opaque
- `hippopotamus.nie` - NIE still image (36×28, v1-bn4), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data`
- `animated-red-blue.nia` - NIA animated container (64×48, v1-bn4, four
  frames, LoopCount 3), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`; FORMAT-03
  verified frame-zero behavior and ANIM-01 verifies nïA multi-frame animation
- `muybridge.gif` - animated GIF multi-frame fixture (source
  `../wuffs/test/data/`); ANIM-01 animation characterization
- `animated-red-blue.gif` - animated GIF disposal/bounds/duration oracle
  (source `../wuffs/test/data/`); ANIM-01 animation characterization
- `gif.animation.golden.manifest` - small golden manifest selecting the two
  verified GIF animation fixtures and recording the CRC-32 (IEEE) of each
  frame's full-canvas straight RGBA pixels after DecodeFrame on a fresh
  zeroed canvas sized from Probe geometry (see Checksums below); generated
  by `go run ./scripts/gen_animation_golden.go`
- `scripts/gen_animation_golden.go` - generator for the animation golden
  manifests above (GIF and NIE); structured so later tasks can extend it to
  further manifests
- `nie.golden.manifest` - small golden manifest selecting the six NIE stills
  plus the NIA container and recording reported dimensions, wire pixel
  encoding, and the canonical CRC-32 (IEEE) of the independently derived
  frame-zero straight RGBA pixels (see Checksums below)
- `nie.animation.golden.manifest` - small golden manifest selecting the
  `animated-red-blue.nia` nïA container and recording the CRC-32 (IEEE) of
  each frame's full-canvas straight RGBA pixels after DecodeFrame on a
  fresh zeroed canvas sized from Probe geometry (see Checksums below);
  generated by `go run ./scripts/gen_animation_golden.go`
- `mona-lisa.21x32.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (23×32, no alpha, l_count 5,
  portrait), vendored from `../wuffs/test/data`; named after its 21×32
  source PNG, it decodes to 23×32 because the thumbhash dimension codes are
  only 14/18/19/23/26/27/32
- `1QcSHQRnh493V4dIh4eXh1h4kJUI.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (23×32, no
  alpha, l_count 5, portrait), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`; an evanw/thumbhash reference
  example cooked with the 3-byte "\xC3\xBE\xFE" magic
- `2fcZFIB3iId_h3iJh4aIYJ2V8g.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×18, no alpha,
  l_count 4, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`; the only l_count-4 fixture
- `2IqDBQQnxnj0JoLYdM3f8ahpuDeHiHdwZw.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×32,
  alpha, l_count 5, square), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`
- `3OcRJYB4d3h_iIeHeEh3eIhw-j3A.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×23, no
  alpha, l_count 5, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`; the canonical upstream
  thumbhash C test pins its final pixel as 0xFF56632E
- `3PcNNYSFeXh_d3eld0iHZoZgVwh2.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×23, no
  alpha, l_count 5, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`
- `HBkSHYSIeHiPiHh8eJd4eTN0EEQG.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×23, no
  alpha, l_count 5, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`
- `IQgSLYZ6iHePh4h1eFeHh4dwgwg3.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×23, no
  alpha, l_count 5, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`
- `VggKDYAW6lZvdYd6d2iZh_p4GE_k.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×23, no
  alpha, l_count 5, landscape), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`
- `YJqGPQw7sFlslqhFafSE-Q6oJ1h2iHB2Rw.th` - cooked ThumbHash image (32×32,
  alpha, l_count 5, square), vendored from
  `../wuffs/test/data/artificial-thumbhash`; the alpha twin of
  `2IqDBQQnxnj0JoLYdM3f8ahpuDeHiHdwZw.th`
- `th.golden.manifest` - small golden manifest selecting the ten cooked
  ThumbHash fixtures above and recording reported dimensions, the alpha
  presence, l_count, and landscape variant properties, and the canonical
  CRC-32 (IEEE) of each fixture's decoded straight RGBA pixels (see Checksums
  below)

## Verified formats

- PNG, WebP, BMP, GIF, JPEG, NPBM, QOI, TGA, WBMP, ETC2, HNSM, NIE, and TH
  are the verified public format set, each backed by fixtures and integration
  coverage in this directory.
- ETC2 is verified via the six PKM fixtures above (ETC1, ETC1S, ETC2 RGB,
  non-multiple-of-four 21×32 geometry, one-bit alpha, and full
  non-premultiplied alpha); `TestIntegrationETC2DecodeCharacterization` pins
  the FormatETC2 contract, exact dimensions and stride, the canonical
  decoded-pixel CRCs, corrupt/truncated PKM rejection, and zero-allocation
  decode.
- NIE is verified via the four `49.*` v1 encodings (non-premultiplied and
  premultiplied BGRA at 4 and 8 bytes per pixel), the spec's `crude-flag.nie`
  example, `hippopotamus.nie`, and the `animated-red-blue.nia` nïA container;
  `TestIntegrationNIEDecodeCharacterization` pins the FormatNIE contract for
  both the nïE and nïA signatures, exact frame-zero pixels against
  independently derived RGBA oracles, ErrDecode for malformed frame-zero data,
  ErrUnknownFormat for near-signature mutations including the byte-reversed
  sentinel, and zero-allocation decode.
- ThumbHash is verified via `mona-lisa.21x32.th` and the nine
  `artificial-thumbhash` fixtures above, spanning alpha presence (0 and 1),
  orientation (portrait, landscape, square), aspect ratio (18/32, 23/32,
  32/23, 32/32), and encoded coefficient counts (l_count 4 and 5);
  `TestIntegrationTHDecodeCharacterization` pins the FormatTH contract for
  cooked files beginning "\xC3\xBE\xFE", exact Wuffs-derived dimensions,
  canonical decoded-pixel CRCs, ErrDecode for truncated cooked files,
  ErrUnknownFormat for raw payloads without the magic and for near-signature
  mutations, and zero-allocation decode.
- Netpbm (PBM/PGM/PPM) is verified via the P5/P6 fixtures above;
  `TestIntegrationNPBMDecodeCharacterization` pins the FormatNPBM contract,
  exact RGBA pixels, unsupported magic-number/maxval rejection, and
  `TestIntegrationNPBMDecodeRGBAAllocsPerRun` pins zero-allocation decode.
- QOI is verified via the RGB `bricks-color.qoi` fixture (oracle: the
  `bricks-color.png` pixels) and the RGBA `alpha-pixels.qoi` fixture;
  `TestIntegrationQOIDecodeCharacterization` pins the FormatQOI contract and
  exact straight RGBA pixels, and `TestIntegrationQOIDecodeRGBAAllocsPerRun`
  pins zero-allocation decode.
- TGA is verified via the true-color `bricks-color.tga`, indexed-color
  `bricks-nodither.tga`, and grayscale/RLE `bricks-gray.tga` fixtures (oracles:
  the corresponding PNG pixels) plus deterministic in-test fixtures covering
  the complete conservative type/depth/origin/attribute matrix;
  `TestIntegrationTGADecodeCharacterization` pins the FormatTGA contract,
  exact pixels, unsupported-subset rejection, and collision behavior, and
  `TestIntegrationTGADecodeRGBAAllocsPerRun` pins zero-allocation decode.
- WBMP (Type 0) is verified via the single-byte-dimension
  `muybridge-frame-000.wbmp` (30×20) and the multi-byte-width
  `bricks-nodither.wbmp` (160×120) fixtures; the in-test oracle unpacks the
  fixture bitmap bits directly (independent of the wasm decoder) and is pinned
  below by CRC-32, and `TestIntegrationWBMPDecodeCharacterization` pins the
  FormatWBMP contract, exact black-and-white pixels, the canonical-varint
  header matrix, and collision behavior, and
  `TestIntegrationWBMPDecodeRGBAAllocsPerRun` pins zero-allocation decode.

## Checksums

`hat.jpeg.golden.nia.crc32` stores the expected CRC-32 (IEEE) of the decoded
`hat.jpeg` pixels converted to a canonical single-frame NIA v1-bn4 stream. Its
value (0x2298F3CA / 580449226) and the NIA encoder's oracle value for
`bricks-color.png` (0x076CB375 / 124564341) were produced by an encoder
implemented directly from the Wuffs NIE/NIA specification and cross-checked
against the standard library's `image/png` decoder; neither was obtained from
this package's wasm decoder.

The WBMP oracles: the expected decoded RGBA pixels of `muybridge-frame-000.wbmp`
and `bricks-nodither.wbmp` have CRC-32 (IEEE) 0x339C150B (30×20, 2400 bytes)
and 0xDDBF25F3 (160×120, 76800 bytes). Both values were produced by an
independent decoder - the Wuffs v0.4 release C library
(`../wuffs-mirror-release-c/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c`) compiled with gcc -
and reproduced bit-for-bit by the in-test WBMP bit unpacker; neither was
obtained from this package's wasm decoder. The black/white pixels (RGBA
{0,0,0,255} and {255,255,255,255}) are byte-identical in straight-RGBA and
premultiplied layout.

The ETC2 oracles: for each fixture selected by `etc2.golden.manifest`, the
stored CRC-32 (IEEE) is over the width*height*4 straight RGBA bytes that the
host writes into the caller's `image.RGBA` Pix. The values were produced by
an independent C oracle program compiled against the same upstream Wuffs
v0.4 release C library (`../wuffs-mirror-release-c/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c`)
embedded in the wasm guest, using the guest's own decode parameters
(BGRA_PREMUL destination format, blend SRC) and converting to straight RGBA
with the same B/R swap and `(c*255)/a` unpremultiply as the host's
`convertBGRAToStraight`; none were obtained from this package's wasm decoder.
The per-fixture values are listed in the manifest itself.

The NIE oracles: for each fixture selected by `nie.golden.manifest`, the
stored CRC-32 (IEEE) is over the width*height*4 straight RGBA bytes that the
host writes into the caller's `image.RGBA` Pix for frame zero. The values and
the in-test per-pixel oracle were derived directly from the NIE wire format
per `../wuffs/doc/spec/nie-spec.md` and the Wuffs v0.4 pixel-swizzler
arithmetic in `wuffs-mirror-release-c/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c`
(bn4: `color_u32_argb_nonpremul__as__color_u32_argb_premul`, bn8:
`color_u64_argb_nonpremul__as__color_u32_argb_premul`, bp4: copy, bp8:
`color_u64__as__color_u32` high bytes), mirrored by the B/R swap and
unpremultiply `(c*255)/a` of the host's `convertBGRAToStraight`; none were
obtained from this package's wasm decoder. The four `49.*` variants encode
the same image, and bn8/bp4/bp8 decode to byte-identical straight RGBA while
bn4's 8-bit non-premultiplied quantisation differs in 63 of 256 pixels.
The per-fixture values are listed in the manifest itself.

The ThumbHash oracles: for each fixture selected by `th.golden.manifest`,
the stored CRC-32 (IEEE) is over the width*height*4 straight RGBA bytes that
the host writes into the caller's `image.RGBA` Pix. The values were produced
by an independent C oracle program compiled against the same upstream Wuffs
v0.4 release C library (`../wuffs-mirror-release-c/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c`)
embedded in the wasm guest, using the guest's own decode parameters
(BGRA_PREMUL destination format, blend SRC, workbuf = workbuf_len().max_incl)
and converting to straight RGBA with the same B/R swap and `(c*255)/a`
unpremultiply as the host's `convertBGRAToStraight`; none were obtained from
this package's wasm decoder. The oracle was validated against the canonical
upstream thumbhash C test's final-pixel value 0xFF56632E for
`3OcRJYB4d3h_iIeHeEh3eIhw-j3A.th` (that test pins only the final pixel, not a
whole-image CRC). The dimensions, has_alpha, l_count, and is_landscape
variant properties were independently parsed from the payload header per
`../wuffs/std/thumbhash/decode_thumbhash.wuffs`. The per-fixture values are
listed in the manifest itself.

The GIF animation oracles: for each fixture selected by
`gif.animation.golden.manifest`, the stored CRC-32 (IEEE) is over the
full-canvas straight RGBA bytes that the host writes into a fresh zeroed
caller's `image.RGBA` Pix after `DecodeFrame(dst, src, index)`. The values
were recorded from the wasm decoder under test via
`go run ./scripts/gen_animation_golden.go`; the per-frame values are listed
in the manifest itself.
